  "description": "Known legitimate sending and reply-to domains for the most-impersonated Canadian institutions. USE FOR MISMATCH DETECTION ONLY: if a message's visible identity claims to be 'org X' but its From/Reply-To domain is not in org X's set, that is a signal. Never use the inverse — a matching domain does not mean the email is legitimate, because From headers are trivially spoofable. Authentication (SPF/DKIM/DMARC) is the only reliable proof of sender, and is checked separately.",
  "usage_notes": [
    "sending_domains: domains the org's mail is observed to originate from (transactional, marketing, support).",
    "reply_to_domains: domains seen in Reply-To headers — sometimes different from sending domains when ESPs are used.",
    "These lists are NON-AUTHORITATIVE and will drift as orgs change marketing vendors. Treat as heuristic, not ground truth.",
    "When matching, normalize to lowercase and strip subdomains down to the registrable domain (eTLD+1) before comparing — unless a specific subdomain is listed explicitly.",
    "aliases: visible-name strings the org is commonly referred to as in scam display names ('CRA', 'Revenue Canada', etc.). Used by the display-name-vs-domain mismatch detector."
  ],
